    title: "The decline in reading",
    domain: 'Media & Literacy',
    difficulty: 'B2',
    rawText: `The decline in reading is a growing concern. With the rise of digital media, people are spending less time with printed books. This shift impacts our ability to focus and think critically as reading not only enhances vocabulary but also stimulates imagination. However, the convenience of getting quick information from screens often outweighs the effort of reading a book. To combat this trend, it is essential to promote the joy of reading from a young age to ensure that future generations continue to benefit from the rich experiences that books offer.`,
