    title: "The downsides of remote work",
    domain: 'Work & Society',
    difficulty: 'B2',
    rawText: `Remote work has its challenges, one major downside being the lack of social interaction. Working from home can lead to feelings of isolation, as you miss out on the spontaneous conversations with colleagues that are always a feature of fixed workplaces. Moreover, remote work often blurs the line between personal and professional life. Even though you are at home, it is often difficult to switch off from work and maintain a healthy work-life balance. While remote work offers flexibility, it's important to be aware of these potential downsides.`,
